---
import { Picture } from 'astro:assets';
import Profile from '../../layouts/Profile.astro';
import { person, site } from '../../data/site';
import { siwes, study, strengths } from '../../data/engineering';
import portrait from '../../assets/photos/portrait-eng-headshot.jpg';
---

<Profile
  path="engineering"
  title={`About · ${person.fullName}, Civil & Environmental Engineering Graduate`}
  description={`About ${person.fullName}: Civil and Environmental Engineering graduate (Environmental option) from the University of Port Harcourt with field experience in project monitoring and research in solid waste management.`}
>
  <div class="wrap about">
    <header class="about-head">
      <p class="label">Engineering · About</p>
      <h1>Careful fieldwork, clear records, and an interest in what happens to waste.</h1>
    </header>

    <figure class="about-photo">
      <Picture
        src={portrait}
        alt={`${person.fullName} in round glasses, a white shirt, dark waistcoat and striped tie, in front of the Department of Civil Engineering sign`}
        widths={[320, 520, 760]}
        sizes="(min-width: 56rem) 28vw, 80vw"
        formats={['avif', 'webp']}
      />
    </figure>

    <div class="prose text">
      <p class="lead">
        I’m {person.fullName}. I studied Civil and Environmental Engineering at the University of Port Harcourt, took
        the Environmental Engineering option, and have defended my final-year project.
      </p>
      <p>
        My industrial training placed me in the {siwes.department} at the {siwes.org}’s Rivers State office from{' '}
        {siwes.period}. On site I supported handovers of emergency solar street-light projects, helped check plinth dimensions and earthing on installed lights, measuring finished roads with a wheel and tape,
        and reconciling all of it against the Bill of Engineering Measurement and Evaluation. Back in the office I helped
        value completed projects and compiled the inspection records, evaluation forms and photographs.
      </p>
      <p>
        For my final-year research I went into two university hostels and measured their waste directly: {study.design.totalKg} kg,
        sorted by hand into nine categories over six days. I then worked out what that waste could become, through
        composting, recycling or energy recovery, and what it costs the climate if it is simply dumped. The female hostel produced
        about five times more waste per person than the male hostel, and plastics made up around four-fifths of it in both.
      </p>
      <p>
        I am looking for an entry-level role in environmental engineering, civil and infrastructure project delivery,
        waste management or sustainability, where careful fieldwork and clear documentation feed into decisions.
      </p>

      <h2>What I am good at</h2>
      <ul>{strengths.map((s) => <li>{s}</li>)}</ul>

      <h2>The other half of my work</h2>
      <p>
        I am also a self-taught web developer and have built production web applications on contract. If that is
        relevant to you, it has <a href="/software">its own profile on this site</a>.
      </p>

      <div class="actions">
        <a class="btn" href="/engineering/contact">Contact me</a>
        <a class="btn btn--quiet" href={site.cv.engineering} download>Download engineering CV</a>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</Profile>

<style>
  .about {
    display: grid;
    gap: var(--space-xl);
    padding-top: var(--space-2xl);
  }

  .about-head {
    display: grid;
    gap: var(--space-m);
  }

  h1 {
    font-size: var(--step-4);
    max-width: 18em;
  }

  .about-photo {
    max-width: 24rem;
  }

  .about-photo :global(img) {
    aspect-ratio: 1;
    object-fit: cover;
    border: 1.5px solid var(--en-text);
  }

  .text h2 {
    font-family: var(--font-sans);
    font-size: 0.78rem;
    font-weight: 600;
    letter-spacing: 0.14em;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    color: var(--accent);
    margin-top: 2.5em;
  }

  .actions {
    display: flex;
    flex-wrap: wrap;
    gap: var(--space-s);
    margin-top: 2em;
  }

  @media (min-width: 56rem) {
    .about {
      grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 1fr) minmax(0, 1.6fr);
      column-gap: var(--space-3xl);
    }
    .about-head {
      grid-column: 1 / -1;
    }
    .about-photo {
      position: sticky;
      top: 8rem;
      align-self: start;
    }
  }
</style>
